    "dv01": {
      "rel": 0.02,
      "tolerance_reason": "Both sides price the Tsiveriotis-Fernandes convertible on a binomial lattice: QuantLib at 17536 steps and Finstack at 1096 steps. The reference DV01 is a central difference over 10bp either side, per bp: QuantLib's lattice price is not smooth in the rate at 1bp, and its own 1bp DV01 moves by 1.6% between 1096, 4384 and 17536 steps, while the 10bp estimate is stable to 0.1%. Finstack's DV01 is a 1bp bump on a 1096-step lattice, so the bound is the 1bp estimator's dispersion."
    },
    "npv": {
      "rel": 0.0001,
      "tolerance_reason": "Canonical Tsiveriotis-Fernandes (1998) two-component (U, V) regression target verified against an independent 1096-step Python TF98 reference (1074398.01, within 0.02% terminal-cell smoothing difference; QuantLib 1.43 BinomialCRRConvertibleEngine blended-rate (V, p) yields 1071424.15). Tight 1e-4 relative band locks exact TF98 regression."
    }
